Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::work_in_flight_is_always_not_ready`.

The defect: `generation_outcome` holds off only while a generation is in flight and forgets the
reseed, so a `RAND_RDY` latched from the last generation is served while `STAT.RAND_RESEEDING`
says the core is being reseeded underneath it.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(generation_outcome(status, interrupt_status, random_numbers), GenerationOutcome::NotReady)`:
a seeded core in 256-bit mode with `RAND_RESEEDING` set and `RAND_RDY` latched returns `Ready`.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -449,5 +449,5 @@ pub fn generation_outcome(
     if interrupt_status & INTERRUPT_STATUS_LINEAR_FEEDBACK_SHIFT_REGISTER_LOCKUP != 0 {
         GenerationOutcome::Lockup
-    } else if status & STATUS_GENERATING != 0 || status & STATUS_RESEEDING != 0 {
+    } else if status & STATUS_GENERATING != 0 {
         GenerationOutcome::NotReady
     } else if status & STATUS_SEEDED == 0 {
